<title>UK: Pegasus to buy software firm for 6.7 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Pegasus to buy software firm for 6.7 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British software firm Pegasus Group Plc said on Thursday it agreed to buy accounting software company CSM from Microvitec Plc for a total of 6.7 million stg.</p>
<p>Pegasus also reported a pretax profit of 1.35 million stg before one-off costs for 1996 versus 893,000 stg in the previous year.</p>
<p>Pegasus' shares were marked up 1.5p at 378.5, while Microvitec's shares were off 0.25p at 28.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
